	<key>dino.friends.privacyBody</key>
	<string>Your clocks and progress are stored on this device. Your name comes from your Game Center account. Friends are optional. Apple manages sign-in, friendships, display names and avatars. The first time an adult turns on Game Center, friends access and result sharing turn on together. Only friends Apple permits are shown. Either switch can be turned off without another question. Turning a switch back on asks the question again. Friends’ data is held in memory and cleared when the app goes into the background, access changes, or you turn off friends.

If you enable iCloud sync, only your level results, measured playing times, stars and game progress are shared through your own iCloud account between your devices. Your dino colors, clocks and settings stay on this device. Turning it off stops new iCloud updates on this device; it does not delete previously saved cloud progress.

While sharing is on, the game sends best level results, measured playing times, stars and progress to Apple Game Center leaderboards. These results may be visible to other Game Center players according to Apple’s settings; the app does not offer private, friends-only storage. Your date of birth, location, email and phone number are never uploaded by this game. No chat, custom messages, ads, analytics or tracking are included.

You can stop future uploads on this device. Published scores are retained by Apple; stopping sharing or resetting the local game does not delete them. Visibility, reporting, friendships and Apple data requests are managed through Apple Games, Game Center and Apple’s privacy controls. Publishing again can restore your previous best results.

Restricted and underage accounts cannot publish progress through this game. A parental gate does not replace legally required parental consent.</string>
